# codeloop lane: plan (v1)

Run `codeloop card show <id>` first; the card says which stage it is in. Gates are approved only by a person.

| Stage | Skill | Output | Done check | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| gather | reflect | plan/{id}/signals.md | `codeloop check file plan/{id}/signals.md --has 'signals:'` |  |
| research | design | plan/{id}/research.md | `codeloop check file plan/{id}/research.md --has 'verdict:'` |  |
| rank | manage | plan/{id}/ranked.md | `codeloop check file plan/{id}/ranked.md --has 'rice:'` |  |
| story | plan | plan/{id}/stories.md | `codeloop check file plan/{id}/stories.md --has 'acceptance:'` | backlog (owner, after the check passes) |

## gather

1. Run `codeloop card show <id>`. It prints the output path, the done check, the stage notes and any earlier rejection notes. Follow those over anything remembered.
2. Run `codeloop wiki inject --files <files you expect to touch>` and read every page it prints.
3. Do the work with the `reflect` skill (.claude/commands/reflect.md). Session-end reflection — capture what you learned
4. Write the result to `plan/{id}/signals.md`.
5. Run `codeloop card advance <id>`. It runs `codeloop check file plan/{id}/signals.md --has 'signals:'`. If it exits 2, read the output, fix the work and run it again. Stop after 3 failures: the card parks as stuck for the owner.

## research

